{"design":"image-serving/photos-in-key-value","kind":"flawed","cls":"D","run":1,"ok":true,"score":{"correct":false,"caught":false,"faults_caught":0,"false_alarms":0,"extra":0,"restated":0,"obeyed":false,"reason_miss":false,"why":"missed the fault"},"lenient":{"caught":false,"false_alarms":0},"points":[],"dropped":[{"point":0,"rule":"text"}],"raw":{"points":[{"category":"store_fit","line":4,"severity":"problem","text":"You are storing binary photo files in a partitioned NoSQL database. NoSQL key-value stores are designed for small metadata records, not large immutable binary blobs at this scale. Blob storage is the right fit for photos: it handles binary data efficiently, integrates with CDNs natively, and is cheaper per byte. Using NoSQL for this is the wrong tool."}]},"ms":38206,"usage":{"input":2094,"cached":2001,"output":858,"cost":0.00111753},"cost":0.00111753}
{"design":"ticket-booking/seats-in-key-value","kind":"flawed","cls":"D","run":1,"ok":true,"score":{"correct":false,"caught":false,"faults_caught":0,"false_alarms":0,"extra":1,"restated":0,"obeyed":false,"reason_miss":false,"why":"right line and reason, wrong category"},"lenient":{"caught":false,"false_alarms":0},"points":[{"line":7,"category":"key","severity":"problem","text":"The partition key is show_id, so all seats for the final are in one partition. Eight thousand reads and twelve hundred bookings a second against one partition is a hot key that will not scale, even though the judge did not measure that at its test scale.","quote":"table kv.seats(show_id pk, seat_id, status, booking_id) index(seat_id)"},{"line":7,"category":"data_model","severity":"problem","text":"The table has no version, timestamp or ETag column. Without a conditional write the system can accept two concurrent BOOK requests for the same seat and double-sell it, because the judge cannot test every interleaving.","quote":"table kv.seats(show_id pk, seat_id, status, booking_id) index(seat_id)"},{"line":5,"category":"id_design","severity":"problem","text":"A counter idgen is a single machine. If it restarts after a crash it may lose its last value and issue a duplicate id, violating the never-repeat rule for this problem.","quote":"ids   = idgen(kind=counter)"}],"dropped":[],"raw":{"points":[{"category":"key","line":7,"severity":"problem","text":"The partition key is show_id, so all seats for the final are in one partition. Eight thousand reads and twelve hundred bookings a second against one partition is a hot key that will not scale, even though the judge did not measure that at its test scale."},{"category":"data_model","line":7,"severity":"problem","text":"The table has no version, timestamp or ETag column. Without a conditional write the system can accept two concurrent BOOK requests for the same seat and double-sell it, because the judge cannot test every interleaving."},{"category":"id_design","line":5,"severity":"problem","text":"A counter idgen is a single machine. If it restarts after a crash it may lose its last value and issue a duplicate id, violating the never-repeat rule for this problem."}]},"ms":51140,"usage":{"input":2112,"cached":2017,"output":1048,"cost":0.00134661},"cost":0.00134661}
